Presently, the only level you have in common with the ghost is that
single level.  If a notepad were found, it would only be useful in
giving information about the present level.

Since one could use a physical notepad next to your desk, I would vote
for an intrinsic object that cannot be burned, dropped, spindled or
mutilated as part of the game.  Who would ever use a scroll of charging
to recharge a notepad when all the notes could be kept on paper?

One problem with a notepad is a size limitation.  Perhaps the notepad
could be implemented as a separate file in the user's home directory
with its title keyed to the name of the save file for startup.  That way
you are limited in your ramblings to your quota.  It could be implemented
as a simple shell out to an editor on this file.
